WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:43.640
After Diana being accidentally drunk,

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.770
Mrs. Barry refused to let them meet.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:51.160
Anne was in the depths of despair,

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:55.020
and she could not perk up
for study or cooking.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:48.200
Diana?!

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.500
Is your mother still angry at me?

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:04.980
And, Anne, she says I'm never
to play with you again.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:10.460
I've cried and cried and I told her
it wasn't your fault...

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:13.020
But it wasn't any use.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:17.470
Then... Then we can never meet again?

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:24.930
I had ever such a time coaxing her to let
me come down and say good-bye to you.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.730
She said I was only to stay ten minutes

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.160
and she's timing me by the clock.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.160
What a tragedy.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:40.640
But... But... what can we do, Anne?

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.140
What can we do?

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.980
I understand, Diana.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.580
But ten minutes isn't very long
to say an eternal farewell in.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:17.430
Diana, will you promise faithfully never to
forget me, the friend of your youth,

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:21.130
no matter what dearer friends may caress thee?

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.240
Indeed I will.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:27.220
And I'll never have another bosom friend.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:28.590
I don't want to have.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:31.870
I couldn't love anybody as I love you.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.630
Oh, Diana...

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.400
Do you LOVE me?

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.280
Why, of course I do.
Didn't you know that?

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:49.720
I thought you LIKED me of course but
I never hoped you LOVED me.

00:04:55.970 --> 00:05:01.670
Why, Diana, I didn't think
anybody could love me.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:06.020
Nobody ever has loved me
since I can remember.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:08.470
Oh, this is wonderful!

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:13.300
It's a ray of light which will forever shine on
the darkness of a path severed from thee.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.530
Oh, just say it once again.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.090
I love you devotedly, Anne.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:22.390
And I always will.
You may be sure of that.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:29.360
And I will always love thee, Diana.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:37.790
In the years to come thy memory will
shine like a star over my lonely life,

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:40.750
as that last story we read together says.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:46.880
Diana, wilt thou give me a lock
of thy jet-black tresses

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:49.890
in parting to treasure forevermore?

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.490
Of my hair?

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.110
Have you got anything to cut it with?

00:05:57.110 --> 00:06:02.050
I've got my patchwork scissors in
my apron pocket fortunately.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:19.470
Fare thee well, my beloved friend.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:25.640
Henceforth we must be as strangers
though living side by side.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:31.090
But my heart will ever be faithful to thee.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.190
I must go.

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:14.970
It is all over.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:28.250
I shall never have another friend.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:31.180
I'm really worse off than ever before,

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:34.310
for I haven't Katie
Maurice and Violetta now.

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:39.990
And even if I had it wouldn't be the same.

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:45.730
Somehow, little dream girls
are not satisfying after a real friend.

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:56.800
Diana and I had such an affecting
farewell down by the spring.

00:08:57.350 --> 00:09:00.720
It will be sacred in my memory forever.

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:08.000
I used the most pathetic language I
could think of and said 'thou' and 'thee.'

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:13.410
'Thou' and 'thee' seem so
much more romantic than 'you.'

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:17.010
Diana gave me a lock of her hair.

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:23.470
I'm going to sew it up in a little bag
and wear it around my neck all my life.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:28.190
Please see that it is buried with me.

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:34.160
For I don't believe I'll live very long.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:39.490
Perhaps when she sees me
lying cold and dead before her

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:42.930
Mrs. Barry may feel remorse
for what she has done

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:46.340
and will let Diana come to my funeral.

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:53.650
I don't think there is much fear of your
dying of grief as long as you can talk, Anne.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:21.700
But that made me feel more relieved.
She still talks all the time.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:25.720
I think it helps her to overcome
her difficulties by talking like that.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:29.960
Well now... She is a very strong girl.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:35.330
But I never thought Mrs. Barry
would be so unreasonable.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:37.870
That's true.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.970
I'm going back to school.

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:03.670
That is all there is left in life for me,

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:07.810
now that my friend has
been ruthlessly torn from me.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:14.800
In school I can look at her
and muse over days departed.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:21.330
Well, you'd better muse
over your lessons and sums.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.200
If you're going back to school

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:27.620
I hope we'll hear no more of breaking slates
over people's heads and such carryings on.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:31.120
Behave yourself and do just
what your teacher tells you.

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:34.700
I'll try to be a model pupil.

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:37.680
There won't be much fun in it, I expect.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:42.360
Mr. Phillips said Minnie Andrews
was a model pupil

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:46.040
and there isn't a spark
of imagination or life in her.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:50.440
She is just dull and poky and
never seems to have a good time.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:56.520
But I feel so depressed that
perhaps it will come easy to me now.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:58.920
Really, give me that basket.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:00.280
You will need to take lunch, right?

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.900
Oh! Please.

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:05.980
I'm going round by the road.

00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:09.660
I couldn't bear to go by
the Birch Path all alone.

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:14.190
I should weep bitter tears if I did.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.240
I will see you later.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:32.800
What a kind of turning point was that?

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:41.300
And I was wondering when she would
return to school as Rachel had said.

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:44.290
Anyway, this helped me a great deal.

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:45.910
Right.

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:27.200
The school had not changed.

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:29.450
The words on the wall,

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:32.520
the traces of knives on the desks,

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:34.660
the trees behind school

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:37.280
and the Lake of Shining Waters.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:40.580
Although with no milk bottles.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:44.210
However, before Anne came back,

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:49.470
the scene changed due to seasons,
and made Anne feel that was different.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.050
Isn't that Anne?

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:53.920
Anne is finally back!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:54.830
Anne!

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:56.460
We were really worried about you!

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:57.580
It's true!

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:01.260
Anne's insecurity was wiped away soon.

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:04.330
Anne was welcomed back to
school with open arms.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:07.370
Her imagination had been
sorely missed in games,

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:09.510
her voice in the singing

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:16.100
and her dramatic ability in the perusal
aloud of books at dinner hour.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.860
But of course, not by everyone.

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:20.720
I don't understand why so
much noise just because of her.

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:23.640
Did she get them drunk?

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:30.520
Some girls were even talking about
Anne intoxicating Diana.

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:31.350
We will talk again later.

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:31.600
Later.
We will talk again later.

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:32.600
Later.

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:40.960
When she got inside, and saw Diana
avoiding her, Anne felt determined.

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:44.780
Good morning, teacher!

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:48.080
Anne Shirley, you are finally back!

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:49.980
I have a favor to ask you, sir.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:50.990
What is it?

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:53.990
It's about our seating.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:54.880
Oh?

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:58.130
I would like to sit with Minnie Andrews.

00:14:58.140 --> 00:14:59.650
What is she thinking?

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:02.840
Could she want to be a model student?

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.020
As you wish.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:06.450
Just by that sentence alone,

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:10.600
I know why you have returned to school.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:14.570
Alright, I shall also forget
whatever that has happened.

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:17.360
I hope you don't forget what you have said,

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:20.750
and work with Minnie Andrews as your target.

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:22.620
Yes, Mr. Philips.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:28.560
She is taunting you, Diana.

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:34.010
Pleased to meet you.

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:35.330
Likewise.

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:49.370
Anne's heart ached at the thought
of Diana not looking at her.

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:54.080
So she determined to study harder.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:04.560
Ruby!

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:12.460
And Sophia Sloane gave me an enormous

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:15.380
yellow pansy cut from the
covers of a floral catalogue.

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:17.440
It's great for desk decoration.

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:21.640
Katie Boulter gave me a perfume bottle
to keep slate water in.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.430
Look, Marilla!

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:28.590
It's wonderful to see that
everyone still likes me.

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.280
And there is more!

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:35.600
Ella May MacPherson offered to teach me a
pattern of knit lace for trimming aprons.

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:40.520
But the most touching present
was from Julia Bell.

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:44.820
She wrote a poem for me.

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:46.280
For Anne.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:50.740
When twilight drops her curtain down
And pins it with a star

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:53.770
Remember that you have a friend

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:56.590
Though she may wander far.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:01.470
Don't you think it's so nice to be appreciated?

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:03.300
Right.

00:17:04.090 --> 00:17:05.860
And what about Diana?

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:10.770
Oh! About that Marilla...
Even you are thinking about Diana.

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:11.770
A little.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:16.290
Diana wouldn't even look at me.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:19.670
She should smile at me at least.

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:25.450
When twilight drops her curtain down

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.640
And pins it with a star

00:17:28.930 --> 00:17:31.910
Remember, remember

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.930
That you have a friend

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:36.670
You have a friend

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:41.010
Though she may wander far

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.900
You're still reading?
This isn't good for your health.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.770
Yes, I will rest soon.

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:22.280
Really? It's already late. Go to sleep now!

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:09.480
The girls were not the only scholars
who welcomed Anne back to School.

00:19:10.030 --> 00:19:11.670
After dinner hour,

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:13.720
when Anne went to her seat,

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:18.160
she found on her desk a
big luscious strawberry apple.

00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:21.710
Who gave me this? Looks delicious!

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:29.860
In Gil's orchard,
there are strawberry apple trees.

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:54.450
Anne Shirley.

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:58.540
Well... I...

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:01.160
You can have this.

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:02.160
Oh!

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:03.470
Charlie Sloane!

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:05.720
Please use this slate pencil.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:08.990
I'm happy.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:14.160
This costs two cents, doesn't it?

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:16.770
It's one of the best.

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:20.290
Thank you, Charlie. I'll use it with care.

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:22.970
That's great!

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:30.360
I'm sorry!

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.340
It's all right!

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:44.830
Charlie Sloane's slate pencil had a better
reception than Gilbert Blythe's apple.

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:50.090
Anne rewarded the donor with a smile
which exalted the infatuated youth

00:20:50.190 --> 00:20:53.140
and caused him to make such
fearful errors in his dictation

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:57.230
that Mr. Phillips kept him in
after school to rewrite it.

00:20:58.530 --> 00:21:01.240
And in the afternoon...

00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:22.610
Diana!

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.680
It's been a long time, Anne.

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:34.810
Mother says I'm not to play with you
or talk to you even in school.

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:38.100
It isn't my fault and don't be cross at me,

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:41.740
because I love you as much as ever.

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:46.050
I miss you awfully to tell all my secrets to.

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:49.390
I don't like Gertie Pye one bit.

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:53.620
I made you one of the new
bookmarkers out of tissue paper.

00:21:55.170 --> 00:22:00.860
They are awfully fashionable now and only
three girls in school know how to make them.

00:22:01.530 --> 00:22:03.660
When you look at it remember

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:07.290
Your true friend: Diana Barry.

00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:26.430
My own darling Diana,

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:32.350
of course I am not cross at you because
you have to obey your mother.

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:36.040
Our spirits can commune.

00:22:36.610 --> 00:22:40.020
I shall keep your lovely present forever.

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:45.610
Minnie Andrews is a very nice little girl,
although she has no imagination.

00:22:46.180 --> 00:22:51.780
But after having been Diana's bosom
friend I cannot be Minnie's.

00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:58.400
Please excuse mistakes because my
spelling isn't very good yet,

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:01.000
although much improoved.

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.350
Yours until death do us part.

00:23:04.350 --> 00:23:07.840
Anne or Cordelia Shirley.

00:23:23.890 --> 00:23:30.040
P.S. I shall sleep with your letter
under my pillow tonight.

00:23:30.040 --> 00:23:32.290
Anne or Cordelia.

00:24:17.590 --> 00:24:22.080
On a certain snowy night, Minnie May
gets ill and Diana asks for help.

00:24:22.280 --> 00:24:25.330
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:25.330 --> 00:24:27.700
Anne Rescues Minnie May.

00:24:27.700 --> 00:24:29.040
Please watch!
